IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`

-- Schedule 7 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376): the activities and descriptors by which a claimant's
-- limited capability for work and work-related activity is assessed (regulation 40(2)(a)), and the facts a claimant states
-- about them for regulations 40(3), 40(4) and 40A.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies a slice of line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- Schedule 7 scores nothing: a descriptor either applies or does not. Descriptors 1 to 14 are single; 15 and 16 have
-- four limbs (a) to (d), each a descriptor of its own (regulation 40(3) says "15(a), 15(b), 15(c), 15(d)").

§ `Schedule 7 — Assessment of whether a claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- src:2744 | SCHEDULE 7 — Assessment of whether a claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity

-- src:2744 | SCHEDULE 7 — Assessment of whether a claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity
-- src:2745 | | Activity | Descriptors |
-- src:2746 | 1. Mobilising unaided by another person with or without a walking stick, manual wheelchair or other aid if such aid is normally or could reasonably be worn or used.
-- src:2746 | 1 Cannot either:(a) mobilise more than 50 metres on level ground without stopping in order to avoid significant discomfort or exhaustion; or(b) repeatedly mobilise 50 metres within a reasonable timescale because of significant discomfort or exhaustion.
-- src:2747 | 2. Transferring from one seated position to another.
-- src:2747 | 2 Cannot move between one seated position and another seated position located next to one another without receiving physical assistance from another person.
-- src:2748 | 3. Reaching.
-- src:2748 | 3 Cannot raise either arm as if to put something in the top pocket of a coat or jacket.
-- src:2749 | 4. Picking up and moving or transferring by the use of the upper body and arms (excluding standing, sitting, bending or kneeling and all other activities specified in this Schedule).
-- src:2749 | 4 Cannot pick up and move a 0.5 litre carton full of liquid.
-- src:2750 | 5. Manual dexterity.
-- src:2750 | 5 Cannot press a button (such as a telephone keypad) with either hand or cannot turn the pages of a book with either hand.
-- src:2751 | 6. Making self understood through speaking, writing, typing, or other means which are normally, or could reasonably be, used unaided by another person.
-- src:2751 | 6 Cannot convey a simple message, such as the presence of a hazard.
-- src:2752 | 7. Understanding communication by:(i) verbal means (such as hearing or lip reading) alone;(ii) non-verbal means (such as reading 16 point print or Braille) alone; or(iii) a combination of sub-paragraphs (i) and (ii),using any aid that is normally, or could reasonably, be used unaided by another person.
-- src:2752 | 7 Cannot understand a simple message, such as the location of a fire escape, due to sensory impairment.
-- src:2753 | 8. Absence or loss of control whilst conscious leading to extensive evacuation of the bowel and/or voiding of the bladder, other than enuresis (bed-wetting), despite the wearing or use of any aids or adaptations which are normally or could reasonably be worn or used.
-- src:2753 | 8 At least once a week experiences:(a) loss of control leading to extensive evacuation of the bowel and/or voiding of the bladder; or(b) substantial leakage of the contents of a collecting device sufficient to require the individual to clean themselves and change clothing.
-- src:2754 | 9. Learning tasks.
-- src:2754 | 9 Cannot learn how to complete a simple task, such as setting an alarm clock, due to cognitive impairment or mental disorder.
-- src:2755 | 10. Awareness of hazard.
-- src:2755 | 10 Reduced awareness of everyday hazards, due to cognitive impairment or mental disorder, leads to a significant risk of:(a) injury to self or others; or(b) damage to property or possessions,such that the claimant requires supervision for the majority of the time to maintain safety.
-- src:2756 | 11. Initiating and completing personal action (which means planning, organisation, problem solving, prioritising or switching tasks).
-- src:2756 | 11 Cannot, due to impaired mental function, reliably initiate or complete at least two sequential personal actions.
-- src:2757 | 12. Coping with change.
-- src:2757 | 12 Cannot cope with any change, due to cognitive impairment or mental disorder, to the extent that day to day life cannot be managed.
-- src:2758 | 13. Coping with social engagement, due to cognitive impairment or mental disorder.
-- src:2758 | 13 Engagement in social contact is always precluded due to difficulty relating to others or significant distress experienced by the claimant.
-- src:2759 | 14. Appropriateness of behaviour with other people, due to cognitive impairment or mental disorder.
-- src:2759 | 14 Has, on a daily basis, uncontrollable episodes of aggressive or disinhibited behaviour that would be unreasonable in any workplace.
-- src:2760 | 15. Conveying food or drink to the mouth.
-- src:2760 | 15(a) Cannot convey food or drink to the claimant's own mouth without receiving physical assistance from someone else;
-- src:2760 | (b) Cannot convey food or drink to the claimant's own mouth without repeatedly stopping or experiencing breathlessness or severe discomfort;
-- src:2760 | (c) Cannot convey food or drink to the claimant's own mouth without receiving regular prompting given by someone else in the claimant's presence; or
-- src:2760 | (d) Owing to a severe disorder of mood or behaviour, fails to convey food or drink to the claimant's own mouth without receiving:(i) physical assistance from someone else; or(ii) regular prompting given by someone else in the claimant's presence.
-- src:2761 | 16. Chewing or swallowing food or drink.
-- src:2761 | 16(a) Cannot chew or swallow food or drink;
-- src:2761 | (b) Cannot chew or swallow food or drink without repeatedly stopping or experiencing breathlessness or severe discomfort;
-- src:2761 | (c) Cannot chew or swallow food or drink without repeatedly receiving regular prompting given by someone else in the claimant's presence; or
-- src:2761 | (d) Owing to a severe disorder of mood or behaviour, fails to:(i) chew or swallow food or drink; or(ii) chew or swallow food or drink without regular prompting given by someone else in the claimant's presence.
@ref Sch 7 (src:2744-2761)
DECLARE `Sch 7 descriptor` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 7 descriptor 1`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 2`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 3`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 4`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 5`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 6`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 7`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 8`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 9`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 10`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 11`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 12`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 13`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 14`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 15(a)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 15(b)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 15(c)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 15(d)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 16(a)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 16(b)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 16(c)`
    `Sch 7 descriptor 16(d)`

-- Where an NHS diagnosis was made: the places regulation 40A(5) lists. A diagnosis counts under regulation 40A(3) only if it was
-- made "in the course of the provision of NHS services", which regulation 40A(5) defines.
-- out of range: the National Health Service Acts and the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 (not among the inputs): in which service the diagnosis was made is a stated input
-- src:797 | (5) In this regulation “NHS services” means—
-- src:798 | (a) health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under—
-- src:799 | (i) section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006;
-- src:800 | (ii) section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006;
-- src:801 | (iii) section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978;
-- src:802 | (b) health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act.
@ref reg 40A(5) (src:797-802)
DECLARE `Services in the course of which a diagnosis was made` HAS
    `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a claimant states about the descriptors. Each list holds descriptors of Schedule 7.
-- The lists answer, one each, the tests of regulations 40(3), 40(4), 40A(2)(b), 40A(3) and 40A(4); the last three fields
-- describe the diagnosis that regulation 40A(3) asks about (one diagnosis is taken to cover every descriptor in the diagnosed
-- lists: fork F-sch7-1).
-- src:774 | (3) In assessing the extent of a claimant's capability to perform any activity listed in Schedule 7, it is a condition that the claimant's incapability to perform the activity arises—
-- src:775 | (a) in respect of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b)—
-- src:776 | (i) from a specific bodily disease or disablement; or
-- src:777 | (ii) as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement; or
-- src:778 | (b) in respect of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d)—
-- src:779 | (i) from a specific mental illness or disablement; or
-- src:780 | (ii) as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement.
-- src:781 | (4) A descriptor applies to a claimant if that descriptor applies to the claimant for the majority of the time or, as the case may be, on the majority of the occasions on which the claimant undertakes or attempts to undertake the activity described by that descriptor.
-- src:786 | (2) A claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant on the basis of an assessment under this Part if—
-- src:787 | (a) the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part (see regulation 40(2)), and
-- src:788 | (b) at least one of the descriptors set out in Schedule 7 constantly applies to the claimant and will do so for the rest of the claimant’s life.
-- src:789 | (3) In assessing the extent of a claimant’s capability to perform any activity listed in Schedule 7, it is a condition that the claimant’s incapability to perform the activity arises—
-- src:790 | (a) in respect of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b), from a specific bodily disease or disablement—
-- src:791 | (i) that the claimant will have for the rest of their life, and
-- src:792 | (ii) that has been diagnosed by an appropriately qualified health care professional in the course of the provision of NHS services, or
-- src:793 | (b) in respect of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d), from a specific mental illness or disablement—
-- src:794 | (i) that the claimant will have for the rest of their life, and
-- src:795 | (ii) that has been diagnosed by an appropriately qualified health care professional in the course of the provision of NHS services.
-- src:796 | (4) A descriptor constantly applies to a claimant if that descriptor applies to the claimant at all times or, as the case may be, on all occasions on which the claimant undertakes or attempts to undertake the activity described by that descriptor.
@ref reg 40(3), 40(4), 40A(2) to (4) (src:774-781) (src:786-796)
DECLARE `Sch 7 claimant facts` HAS
    `descriptors that apply for the majority of the time or on the majority of the occasions`                       IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement`                           IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement`   IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement`                           IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement`     IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors that apply at all times or on all the occasions`                                                   IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors that will so apply for the rest of the claimant's life`                                            IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life`   IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that has been diagnosed`   IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life`   IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that has been diagnosed`   IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor`
    `professional who made the diagnosis`                                                                           IS A Practitioner
    `professional who made the diagnosis is appropriately qualified`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `services in the course of which the diagnosis was made`                                                        IS A `Services in the course of which a diagnosis was made`
